section: rts
synopsis: The RTS now uses the `clock_gettime` monotonic clock on all POSIX platforms.
issues: #28119
mrs: !16968
description:
  Having a good monotonic clock source is vital for concurrent programming.
  Historically platform APIs for high precision monotonic time have not been
  widely available in a consistent standard form, and GHC was forced to depend
  on a hodge podge of different APIs (some of which did not even provide
  monotonic time). POSIX.1-2008 mandated the `clock_gettime` API, and this is
  now old enough and widely supported enough that the RTS can now use this
  with the `CLOCK_MONOTONIC` and `CLOCK_REALTIME` clocks for all of its internal
  timing needs on all POSIX platforms.

  The compatibility implication is that some older POSIX platforms that do not
  support the POSIX.1-2008 standard will no longer be supported. To the best of
  our knowledge the main platforms impacted are versions of macOS prior to
  version 10.12 (released 2016, EOL 2019).
